==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|hann|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gmq-pro|is}} {{term/t|gmq-pro|*hānaʀ}}, of uncertain origin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|stressed}} {{IPA|/ˈhanː/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|anː|lang=is}}
*: {{rfap||is}}
* {{a|unstressed}} {{IPA|/an(ː)/|lang=is}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# {{sense|personal pronoun}} [[he]]
#: '''''Hann''' [[vera#Icelandic|er]] [[gamall]].''
#:: '''He''' [[is]] [[old]].
#: '''''Hann''' [[drepa#Icelandic|drap]] [[hann#Icelandic|hann]].''
#:: '''He''' [[killed]] [[him]].

# {{sense|personal pronoun}} accusative singular form of the word ''[[hann#Icelandic|hann]]'' (meaning "[[he]]") meaning "[[him]]".
#: ''[[hann#Icelandic|Hann]] [[drepa#Icelandic|drap]] '''hann'''.''
#:: [[he|He]] [[killed]] '''him'''.
#: ''[[hætta|Hættu]] þessu! Ég [[elska]] '''hann'''!''
#:: [[stop|Stop]] it! I [[love]] '''him'''!

