==Old Norse==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmq-pro|non}} {{term/t|gmq-pro|*hānaʀ}}, of uncertain origin. Perhaps a compound of {{term/t|gmq-pro|*he-}} (answering to English {{term|he|lang=en}}) and {{term/t|gmq-pro||*ānaʀ}} (from {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*jainaz}}, answering to Gothic {{term|𐌾𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃|tr=jains|lang=got}}) or even directly from {{term/t|gmq-pro||*ānaʀ}} with ''h-'' added due to influence from the demonstrative pronoun {{term|hinn|lang=non}}, or else perhaps directly inherited from Proto-Indo-European and answering to {{etyl|grc|-}} {{term|κεῖνος|tr=keînos|lang=grc}}.

===Pronoun===
{{head|non|pronoun}}
# [[he]] {{qualifier|third-person nominative singular masculine personal pronoun}}

